  "tutorialS1Title": "Getting started with Talia",
  "tutorialS1Cat": "Start",
  "tutorialS1Does": "Talia opens with a short intro, lets you choose the adult or kids path, then takes you to Home. You can use it as a guest and sign in later.",
  "tutorialS1Open": "It appears the first time you open the app. Afterwards, use the bottom bar to move between Home, Quran, Memorization, Adhkar and Progress.",
  "tutorialS1Useful": "Helpful for new users who want the map of the app before reading or memorizing.",
  "tutorialS1Step1": "Go through the intro pages, or tap Skip.",
  "tutorialS1Step2": "Choose the adult or kids path, then continue as a guest or sign in.",
  "tutorialS1Step3": "Use the bottom bar to move between the main sections.",
  "tutorialS1Tip1": "Start from Home: it gathers today's reading, your progress and shortcuts.",
  "tutorialS1Tip2": "You can change the memorization path later in Settings > Quran & Memorization.",
  "tutorialS1Note1": "Signing in is optional. Without it your progress stays on this device.",
  "tutorialS1Note2": "Settings are behind the gear icon at the top of Home.",
  "tutorialS2Title": "Home",
  "tutorialS2Cat": "Start",
  "tutorialS2Does": "Home shows the next prayer, a main card for what to do next, today's wird, your streak and XP, the ayah of the day and your recent activity.",
  "tutorialS2Open": "Tap Home in the bottom bar.",
  "tutorialS2Useful": "The best daily starting point: reading, memorizing and follow-up in one screen.",
  "tutorialS2Step1": "Tap the main card to continue reading, resume a session or open today's plan.",
  "tutorialS2Step2": "Tap \"Something else\" to see other options.",
  "tutorialS2Step3": "Open Settings with the gear icon at the top.",
  "tutorialS2Step4": "Tap \"Choose city\" to set your city for prayer times.",
  "tutorialS2Tip1": "The ring shows the share of the whole Quran you have memorized, so it grows slowly. The seven dots are the last seven days, ending today.",
  "tutorialS2Tip2": "Tap the icons under the ayah of the day to share it, open it in the Mushaf or listen to it.",
  "tutorialS2Note1": "Some cards appear only when there is data, such as a started khatmah or a saved reading position.",
  "tutorialS2Note2": "The account card can be dismissed with the X.",
  "tutorialS3Title": "Reading the Quran",
  "tutorialS3Cat": "Quran",
  "tutorialS3Does": "The Quran tab lists the surahs, the juz and your bookmarks. The reader shows the Mushaf page with tajweed colors, audio, bookmarks and a focus mode.",
  "tutorialS3Open": "Tap Quran, then choose a surah or a juz. You can also open today's wird from Home.",
  "tutorialS3Useful": "For your daily wird, looking up an ayah, or reading before a memorization session.",
  "tutorialS3Step1": "Choose a surah from the list, or use the search box at the top.",
  "tutorialS3Step2": "Swipe to turn the page.",
  "tutorialS3Step3": "Long-press an ayah to listen to it, copy it, bookmark it, share it or start memorizing it.",
  "tutorialS3Step4": "Open the menu with the three dots to go to a page, surah or juz, choose a reciter, switch tajweed colors on or off, or enter focus mode.",
  "tutorialS3Step5": "Stay on a page for a few seconds while reading: it is counted as read automatically.",
  "tutorialS3Tip1": "Listen to an ayah before memorizing it to get the pronunciation right.",
  "tutorialS3Tip2": "The Continue reading card on the Quran tab takes you back to your last page.",
  "tutorialS3Note1": "The Quran text is bundled with the app, so it displays without a connection.",
  "tutorialS3Note2": "Audio needs a connection unless it was already cached.",
  "tutorialS4Title": "Search and bookmarks",
  "tutorialS4Cat": "Quran",
  "tutorialS4Does": "Find a surah by name or an ayah by its words, and keep important ayahs as bookmarks.",
  "tutorialS4Open": "Use the search box at the top of the Quran tab, or the search icon on Home. Bookmarks have their own tab on the Quran screen.",
  "tutorialS4Useful": "For collecting ayahs to review, similar ayahs, or places you want to come back to.",
  "tutorialS4Step1": "Type a surah name or words from an ayah.",
  "tutorialS4Step2": "Open the surah or the ayah from the results.",
  "tutorialS4Step3": "Long-press an ayah in the reader and choose Bookmark.",
  "tutorialS4Step4": "Open the Bookmark tab to return to saved ayahs or remove them.",
  "tutorialS4Tip1": "Bookmark the start of each memorization section to return to it quickly.",
  "tutorialS4Tip2": "Search ignores diacritics, so you can type plain Arabic.",
  "tutorialS4Note1": "Ayah search shows at most 50 results: add more words to narrow it.",
  "tutorialS4Note2": "Removing a bookmark does not affect any reading or memorization progress.",
  "tutorialS5Title": "Memorizing step by step",
  "tutorialS5Cat": "Memorization",
  "tutorialS5Does": "The Memorization tab brings together today's plan, practice by surah, the listening quiz and reviews by recitation. Every ayah goes through learn, memorize and recite.",
  "tutorialS5Open": "Tap Memorization. On first use you choose the adult or kids path.",
  "tutorialS5Useful": "For systematic memorization with spaced reviews, so what you memorize stays.",
  "tutorialS5Step1": "Create a plan, or pick a surah under Practice by Surah.",
  "tutorialS5Step2": "Learn: listen to the ayah and read it.",
  "tutorialS5Step3": "Memorize: try without looking, and use the hints (first word, first letters, show the ayah) only when needed.",
  "tutorialS5Step4": "Recite: record your recitation, or grade yourself honestly if speech recognition is unavailable. A block of ayahs is then recited together.",
  "tutorialS5Tip1": "Hints are recorded and affect when the ayah comes back for review.",
  "tutorialS5Tip2": "Change how strict recitation checking is in Settings > Quran & Memorization > Accuracy level.",
  "tutorialS5Note1": "Leaving a session asks whether to continue later or discard it.",
  "tutorialS5Note2": "Without speech recognition or microphone permission, grading yourself is a fully supported route.",
  "tutorialS6Title": "Daily adhkar and the counter",
  "tutorialS6Cat": "Adhkar",
  "tutorialS6Does": "Morning and evening adhkar, general adhkar and duas, with a repetition counter, an index, free tasbeeh and a smart wird that follows the time of day.",
  "tutorialS6Open": "Tap Adhkar, then choose morning, evening, general adhkar, duas, smart wird or free tasbeeh.",
  "tutorialS6Useful": "For the morning and evening wird, tasbeeh sessions, and sharing a dua quickly.",
  "tutorialS6Step1": "Choose a category; the one for the current time is highlighted at the top.",
  "tutorialS6Step2": "Tap the counter once for each repetition; it moves to the next dhikr when you finish.",
  "tutorialS6Step3": "Open the index to jump to a specific dhikr.",
  "tutorialS6Step4": "Change the text size, copy or share the dhikr when needed.",
  "tutorialS6Step5": "When you finish, reset the session or go back.",
  "tutorialS6Tip1": "Turn on morning and evening reminders in Settings > Notifications.",
  "tutorialS6Tip2": "Press and hold the counter to undo the last count.",
  "tutorialS6Note1": "The adhkar are bundled with the app and work offline.",
  "tutorialS6Note2": "Counters belong to the current day's session; they are not a memorization certificate.",
  "tutorialS7Title": "Daily plan and reviews",
  "tutorialS7Cat": "Memorization",
  "tutorialS7Does": "Your plan serves new ayahs and reviews every day. Reviews return on a schedule based on how well you recited, so what you memorize stays firm.",
  "tutorialS7Open": "Memorization > Continue Today's Plan, or the main card on Home.",
  "tutorialS7Useful": "For steady memorization with smart review instead of relying on memory alone.",
  "tutorialS7Step1": "Open Continue Today's Plan from the Memorization tab.",
  "tutorialS7Step2": "Finish the new ayahs of the day.",
  "tutorialS7Step3": "Do the Review Session when ayahs are due: the badge shows how many.",
  "tutorialS7Step4": "Open View Today's Plan to see what is done and what remains.",
  "tutorialS7Step5": "Try the Listening Quiz once you have memorized a few ayahs: it plays an ayah and asks you to name its surah or continue it.",
  "tutorialS7Tip1": "Grade yourself honestly: it decides how strong the ayah is and when it returns.",
  "tutorialS7Tip2": "If the plan feels heavy, lower the daily ayahs in Plan Settings.",
  "tutorialS7Note1": "On rest days (set by days per week) you get reviews only.",
  "tutorialS7Note2": "The Listening Quiz needs at least five memorized ayahs.",
  "tutorialS8Title": "Setting up your plan",
  "tutorialS8Cat": "Memorization",
  "tutorialS8Does": "Create your plan from a quick preset or from scratch: name, surah range, ayahs per day, days per week, session length, difficulty and reviews.",
  "tutorialS8Open": "Memorization > Create plan, or Plan Settings later.",
  "tutorialS8Useful": "For a specific goal, such as memorizing a particular juz, or planning a child's memorization.",
  "tutorialS8Step1": "Pick a quick preset (Light, Balanced, Intensive, Juz Amma) or fill in the fields yourself.",
  "tutorialS8Step2": "Choose the surah range. Choosing Child takes you to the kids path, where kids plans are managed.",
  "tutorialS8Step3": "Set ayahs per day, days per week and session length.",
  "tutorialS8Step4": "Choose the difficulty and turn near and far revision on or off.",
  "tutorialS8Step5": "Save and start the plan.",
  "tutorialS8Tip1": "The session length limits new ayahs, at about four minutes each. A note appears if the minutes are too short for your goal.",
  "tutorialS8Tip2": "Start small to build a habit, then increase.",
  "tutorialS8Note1": "The plan can be deleted from the setup screen.",
  "tutorialS8Note2": "The finishing time shown on the screen is an estimate.",
  "tutorialS9Title": "Kids mode and parent tools",
  "tutorialS9Cat": "Memorization",
  "tutorialS9Does": "A journey of memorization houses with stars, levels and repeated listening for children, plus parent tools for follow-up.",
  "tutorialS9Open": "Choose the kids path. The parent PIN is set during kids setup. Parent tools appear on Home once you are signed in.",
  "tutorialS9Useful": "For children and beginners, or for a parent who wants to follow stars, sessions and rewards.",
  "tutorialS9Step1": "Choose the kids path, then enter the child's name, age, starting surah and a four-digit parent PIN.",
  "tutorialS9Step2": "On the kids home tap Continue now, listen to the ayah three times, then try from memory.",
  "tutorialS9Step3": "If recording does not work, tap \"I finished memorizing\": the parent enters the PIN to confirm.",
  "tutorialS9Step4": "Follow the journey map: houses open one after another as missions are completed.",
  "tutorialS9Tip1": "Keep the PIN private: it also protects leaving the kids path.",
  "tutorialS9Tip2": "Use the Mushaf tab on the kids home to let the child read in the Quran.",
  "tutorialS9Note1": "Linking a child from another device needs an account.",
  "tutorialS9Note2": "One child per device: more children use their own devices, linked to the guardian.",
  "tutorialS10Title": "Progress, achievements and certificates",
  "tutorialS10Cat": "Progress",
  "tutorialS10Does": "Shows your reading and memorization statistics, your daily streak, achievements, your certificates, and lets you share your progress.",
  "tutorialS10Open": "Tap Progress in the bottom bar.",
  "tutorialS10Useful": "For a weekly review, celebrating achievements and tracking consistency.",
  "tutorialS10Step1": "Review the top cards for streak days, pages read, XP and reviews.",
  "tutorialS10Step2": "Open the reading and memorization sections for pages, ayahs, surahs and juz.",
  "tutorialS10Step3": "Switch the achievement filters between all, reading, memorization and streak.",
  "tutorialS10Step4": "Tap an unlocked achievement for details and sharing.",
  "tutorialS10Step5": "Your certificates appear when you complete a surah, a juz or the whole Quran.",
  "tutorialS10Tip1": "Reading a khatmah counts toward your streak, but not toward free-reading statistics.",
  "tutorialS10Tip2": "Certificates depend on genuinely memorizing the required ayahs.",
  "tutorialS10Note1": "Some statistics appear only after you start memorizing.",
  "tutorialS10Note2": "Sharing happens only when you choose to share.",
  "tutorialS11Title": "Settings, account and notifications",
  "tutorialS11Cat": "Settings",
  "tutorialS11Does": "Gathers your account and profile, language and theme, Quran and memorization settings, prayer times, notifications and information about the app.",
  "tutorialS11Open": "Tap the gear icon on Home.",
  "tutorialS11Useful": "For personalizing the app, protecting your progress and setting reminders that suit your day.",
  "tutorialS11Step1": "Sign in or create an account with an email and password to manage your account.",
  "tutorialS11Step2": "Edit your name under Profile.",
  "tutorialS11Step3": "Choose Arabic or English, and the light, dark, pure black or system theme.",
  "tutorialS11Step4": "Under Quran & Memorization, set background playback and the accuracy level, or reset your path.",
  "tutorialS11Step5": "Under Prayer times, choose your city and calculation method.",
  "tutorialS11Step6": "Under Notifications, turn reminders for reviews, streak, adhkar and prayers on or off.",
  "tutorialS11Tip1": "Write your name in Arabic so it looks right on certificates.",
  "tutorialS11Tip2": "Reset the path under Quran & Memorization to switch between adult and kids.",
  "tutorialS11Note1": "Notifications need the system permission to work.",
  "tutorialS11Note2": "Language and theme are stored on this device.",
  "tutorialS12Title": "Working offline and your data",
  "tutorialS12Cat": "Settings",
  "tutorialS12Does": "The Quran and adhkar texts are bundled with the app. Your progress, plans and settings are stored on the device. With an account, some of it also syncs online.",
  "tutorialS12Open": "There is no separate screen: it works automatically while you use the app.",
  "tutorialS12Useful": "For understanding what works offline and avoiding the loss of important progress.",
  "tutorialS12Step1": "Read the Quran and use the adhkar even without internet.",
  "tutorialS12Step2": "Keep reading and memorizing: progress is saved on the device.",
  "tutorialS12Step3": "Sign in when you want account features or to restore your memorization progress.",
  "tutorialS12Tip1": "On a new device, sign in to restore what your account supports.",
  "tutorialS12Tip2": "Connect to the internet to play recitations that are not cached.",
  "tutorialS12Note1": "Clearing the app's data in system settings removes anything not saved to your account.",
  "tutorialS12Note2": "Signing out removes your khatmah plan and history from this device: they are stored only here.",
  "tutorialS14Note2": "Reliable alerts may need the exact-alarm permission in phone settings.",
  "tutorialS14Note1": "Times are calculated on the device, so they work offline.",
  "tutorialS14Tip2": "If you are unsure which method fits, pick the one your local authority uses.",
  "tutorialS14Tip1": "If your city is not listed, use a custom location: copy its coordinates from a maps app.",
  "tutorialS14Step4": "Turn on prayer calm mode if you want recitation to pause when prayer time starts.",
  "tutorialS14Step3": "Turn on prayer alerts: they switch on automatically the first time you set a location.",
  "tutorialS14Step2": "Choose the calculation method (automatic by country by default) and the Asr calculation.",
  "tutorialS14Step1": "Choose your country and city, or Custom location to enter coordinates.",
  "tutorialS14Useful": "For knowing prayer times wherever you are, with an alert when it is time.",
  "tutorialS14Open": "On Home tap Choose city, or open Settings > Prayer times.",
  "tutorialS14Does": "Shows prayer times and the next prayer on Home, and can alert you at each prayer.",
  "tutorialS14Cat": "Settings",
  "tutorialS14Title": "Prayer times and alerts",
  "tutorialS13Note2": "It is stored only on this device, and is removed when you sign out.",
  "tutorialS13Note1": "The khatmah is separate from free reading: neither moves the other's position.",
  "tutorialS13Tip2": "If you fall behind, use the options on the dashboard to catch up.",
  "tutorialS13Tip1": "You can dedicate the khatmah to someone you love when you create it.",
  "tutorialS13Step4": "If you read from a printed Mushaf, use Record to enter the pages.",
  "tutorialS13Step3": "Read the day's wird: each page you read is recorded.",
  "tutorialS13Step2": "Start the khatmah and tap Continue reading on the dashboard.",
  "tutorialS13Step1": "Choose pages per day or a duration, and optionally a start page.",
  "tutorialS13Useful": "For reading the Quran regularly with a clear goal, such as in Ramadan.",
  "tutorialS13Open": "On Home tap Start your khatmah, or open the khatmah card once you have started one.",
  "tutorialS13Does": "Plan a full reading of the Quran at the pace you choose, by pages per day or by number of days. Talia tracks your progress page by page and keeps a history of completed khatmahs.",
  "tutorialS13Cat": "Quran",
